        "thinking": "The `createEmbeddedPostgresLogBuffer` and `formatEmbeddedPostgresError` are only used in `server/src/index.ts` (the server's entry point), which is NOT included in the CF worker's bundle (the CF worker imports individual route files, not `server/src/index.ts`).\n\nThe `getEmbeddedPostgresTestSupport` and `startEmbeddedPostgresTestDatabase` are only used in tests (the grep didn't find any non-test files).\n\nSo BOTH embedded-postgres-related exports from `@paperclipai/db/index.ts` are safe to remove from the main package export, because:\n\n\n- The test functions are only needed in test files\n- The error formatting functions are only needed in the server's entry point\n\nThe cleanest approach is to remove these exports from the main index and have the importing files use relative imports instead, but I should verify this won't break the server's tests or the entry point's imports first.\n\nActually, the simpler path might be to use package.json export conditions—if Wrangler respects the `browser` or `worker` condition, I could create a conditional export that excludes the embedded-postgres functions for worker environments, avoiding the need to modify multiple files. I'm realizing wrangler v3 supports a custom build command in the config, which would let me use esbuild directly to handle the external dependencies properly without needing wrangler's bundler to process embedded-postgres at all.",
